    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i was reading about box breathing (the 4-4-4-4 thing) and was wondering what it actually does to the body? like how does it affect stress or my nervous system specifically?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, or 4-4-4-4 breathing, primarily shifts your nervous system from a \"fight or flight\" (sympathetic) state to a \"rest and digest\" (parasympathetic) state. This controlled rhythm helps activate the vagus nerve, which is key to calming the body down. By slowing your breath, it signals to your brain that you are safe, thereby reducing the physical manifestations of stress like a racing heart.",
      "source": "target",
